The primary deliverable is a discrete categorical raster where each pixel is assigned the unique identifier (GID) corresponding to its classified IUCN GET Ecosystem Functional Group.

@section(Confidence and Purity Metrics)
Alongside the categorical map, the external pipeline generates secondary rasters:
1. *Confidence Map*: Displays the normalized probability score for the assigned EFG, reflecting how well the underlying spatial data matched the soft rules.
2. *Gini Purity Map:* Provides a metric of class purity, highlighting areas where a pixel strongly qualified for multiple overlapping EFGs.

@section(Limitations)
Because the core algorithm relies on a predefined sequential ranking, mutual exclusivity between highly similar ecosystems is resolved by priority rather than continuous probability. If a pixel technically qualifies for two EFGs, it is permanently assigned to whichever EFG is evaluated first in the sequence, which may occasionally obscure secondary overlapping ecosystems.

@section(Data Dependency)
The accuracy of the mapping, and particularly the effectiveness of the fuzzy confidence scoring, is strictly dependent on the spatial resolution, temporal alignment, and completeness of the input environmental rasters. Areas with significant NoData clustering rely heavily on the post-processing gap-filling routines.

