@section(Sequential Fuzzy Classification)
The external mapping algorithm executes a first-come, first-served classification based on a strict, predefined hierarchical ranking (`mapping_order`). For each EFG in the hierarchy, the model evaluates a pixel against a dictionary of environmental conditions. 

The evaluation relies on a weighted scoring system:
1. *Hard Constraints*: Thematic filters (very important veriables to map a particula EFG) act as strict Boolean masks. Failing these conditions explicitly removes a pixel from consideration for that EFG.
2. *Soft Constraints*: The rest of the variables act as fuzzy modifiers. Failing a soft constraint does not eliminate the pixel but reduces its cumulative confidence score.

@section(Fallback and Gap-Filling)
After the primary sequential loop finishes, the algorithm applies a post-processing gap-filling mechanism. Unclassified pixels are evaluated against known land cover dominance and hydroform associations. The algorithm assigns these remaining pixels to the most probable EFG based on the maximum calculated confidence score derived during the initial evaluation.

