@section(Overview)
This model maps the spatial distribution of the IUCN Global Ecosystem Typology (GET) across all applicable Ecosystem Functional Groups (EFGs). The primary objective is to classify global or regional environmental pixels into specific ecosystems based on an extensive matrix of ecological, climatic, hydrological, and geomorphological conditions.

The classification is carried out using an external, rule-based execution pipeline. It leverages a fuzzy-logic masking engine that processes high-resolution spatial covariates against predefined ecosystem profiles to generate comprehensive categorical maps and confidence metrics.
